<Base title="Architecture: agents, source and live software" description="Original visual explainers for App Composer’s verified environment, pinned independent services and locally encrypted fictional assistant state."><h1>The connections<br/>that make it work.</h1><p class="lede">Three views of the actual system. Each separates authority, executable source and data rather than drawing every service as the same box.</p><section class="section"><h2>The agent runs the work.</h2><svg class="diagram-wide" viewBox="0 0 760 650" width="760" height="650" style="width:100%;height:auto;max-height:650px" role="img" aria-label="MP supplies intent and human approval to external Codex. Codex checks GitHub and Cloudflare, produces an exact source and deployment, and verifies HTTPS. Woodhouse operates this work but is not a customer runtime."><path d="M380 105V560" stroke="#d95022" stroke-width="7" fill="none"/><rect x="180" y="20" width="400" height="100" rx="12" fill="#e6ac7f"/><text x="210" y="62" font-size="27">MP: intent and authority</text><text x="210" y="94" font-size="18">MFA, purchases, consequential approval</text><rect x="180" y="180" width="400" height="130" rx="12" fill="#202923"/><text x="210" y="225" fill="#f4f0e8" font-size="27">External Codex</text><text x="210" y="260" fill="#f4f0e8" font-size="18">Actual workspace · GitHub · Wrangler</text><text x="210" y="289" fill="#f4f0e8" font-size="18">Build, inspect, recover and verify</text><rect x="180" y="370" width="400" height="100" rx="12" fill="#dbe4d4"/><text x="210" y="412" font-size="27">Exact source and deployment</text><text x="210" y="445" font-size="18">Public web requests have no deploy authority</text><rect x="180" y="530" width="400" height="100" rx="12" fill="#264e40"/><text x="210" y="572" fill="#f4f0e8" font-size="27">Verified HTTPS result</text><text x="210" y="605" fill="#f4f0e8" font-size="18">Source identity + real interaction</text></svg><ol class="diagram-mobile"><li><strong>MP: intent and authority</strong><br/>Human authentication and consequential approval.</li><li><strong>External Codex</strong><br/>Checks its workspace, GitHub and Cloudflare tools.</li><li><strong>Exact source and deployment</strong><br/>Builds, tests, publishes within authority.</li><li><strong>Verified HTTPS</strong><br/>Checks identity and real interaction.</li></ol><details><summary>Read the flow in text</summary><p>MP provides intent and only unavoidable human capabilities. The authorised external Codex task verifies its actual repository and Cloudflare tools, builds and tests exact source, deploys within existing authority, then checks HTTPS identity and interaction. The public site cannot inherit those credentials. Woodhouse operates implementation without becoming a customer runtime dependency.</p></details></section><section class="section"><h2>Pin the code. Keep privacy current.</h2><div class="split"><div><h3>Two independent sources</h3><p>Guestbook and Showcase have separate GitHub repositories and standalone Workers. A compatible upstream commit is a candidate, never an automatic replacement for Composer’s mounted code.</p><h3>A composed release</h3><p>The whole composition digest names its integrated services, including dependency pins. The root activates those bindings only after review. Deployment verifies the root and both mounted source identities.</p></div><div class="ink"><h3>One current privacy decision</h3><p>Guestbook owns D1 moderation and private R2 media. Standalone and integrated code read that current app-owned state. Showcase features reference stable item IDs, then resolve current source eligibility.</p><p>Hide or delete a source item and controlled requests revoke it. Restoring an older executable cannot restore a previous approval or a deleted image.</p></div></div><details><summary>Read the update boundary in text</summary><p>GitHub source histories remain independent. The validated composition locks their commits and uses immutable service identities derived from the full input digest. Staging a new dependency cannot mutate an old service. App data remains with its owner. Code rollback restores a reviewed root and pinned services; metadata/media recovery is a separate authorised operation.</p></details></section><section class="section"><h2>The key doesn’t cross.</h2><svg class="diagram-wide" viewBox="0 0 760 480" width="760" height="480" style="width:100%;height:auto" role="img" aria-label="The fictional document is encrypted locally into ciphertext. The owner keeps the passphrase separately. A reviewed selection, without the key or unselected memories, can be explicitly copied to a model."><rect x="45" y="40" width="300" height="150" rx="12" fill="#ded3e8"/><text x="70" y="88" font-size="27">Fictional document</text><text x="70" y="130" font-size="18">Identity, memories, checkpoints</text><path d="M200 190V295" stroke="#594272" stroke-width="7" fill="none"/><rect x="45" y="295" width="300" height="130" rx="12" fill="#594272"/><text x="70" y="340" fill="#f4f0e8" font-size="27">Encrypted export</text><text x="70" y="378" fill="#f4f0e8" font-size="18">Ciphertext may be retained</text><rect x="415" y="40" width="300" height="150" rx="12" fill="#e6ac7f"/><text x="440" y="88" font-size="27">Owner-held passphrase</text><text x="440" y="130" font-size="18">No server or provider receives it</text><rect x="415" y="295" width="300" height="130" rx="12" fill="#264e40"/><text x="440" y="340" fill="#f4f0e8" font-size="27">Reviewed disclosure</text><text x="440" y="378" fill="#f4f0e8" font-size="18">Explicit selection, no key</text></svg><ol class="diagram-mobile"><li><strong>Fictional document</strong><br/>Identity, memories and reviewed checkpoints.</li><li><strong>Local encryption</strong><br/>Owner keeps the passphrase separately.</li><li><strong>Encrypted export</strong><br/>Only ciphertext is retained.</li><li><strong>Explicit disclosure</strong><br/>A reviewed selection crosses; the key does not.</li></ol><details><summary>Read the privacy boundary in text</summary><p>The synthetic document is encrypted locally using AES-GCM and an owner-held passphrase-derived key. The ciphertext export and passphrase stay separate. A different action previews an exact memory subset and requires explicit consent before plaintext clipboard disclosure. Neither the key nor unselected memories is included. No real private-data security assurance or server sync is claimed.</p></details><a href="/state">Open the fictional proof</a></section></Base>
